  "body": "A Discord user (Archades, Australia) runs a **CNC 3D QueenBee v1** router (delrin leadscrew Y; the v2 has a ballscrew Y) on **UCCNC with an AXBB-E** motion controller: 3 axis, 4th rotary possible, UCR201 pendant. The stock controller for this machine would be CNC 3D's Nighthawk. He is interested in 2.5D first, 3D contouring later.\n\nCamCraft has no UCCNC post. UCCNC reads Mach3-style G-code, so `assets/posts/mach4.cps` is the nearest starting point and may already work for plain 2.5D jobs.\n\n**Work**\n- A `uccnc.cps` post, derived from `mach4.cps`. Check UCCNC's published G/M-code list for differences: tool change (M6 handling and macros), arcs (G2/G3 with I/J, plane selection), canned cycles it supports, G28/G53 use, comments, program end, spindle and coolant codes, and A-axis output for the rotary.\n- A QueenBee machine file (`.mch`), with travels from CNC 3D's public specs for the v1/v2 sizes, a router spindle and no tool changer.\n- Golden G-code tests for a facing, pocket, contour and drill job.\n\n**Testing:** Archades can run a test, but material costs him real money, so hand him a short air-cut or foam file only once the goldens pass, and keep it under about 2 minutes.\n\nDone means: `uccnc.cps` and a QueenBee `.mch` are in the library, with golden tests for 2.5D ops; the post refuses anything UCCNC can't run; the machine/post library doc lists both.\n",
